From fe2f359c75d185fdd4ba0ab471984dcad6c6eaf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:54:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add tax configuration for payments: VAT at checkout +
 instructor withholding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New admin-configurable tax_settings (singleton row, editable from Platform
  Settings): vat_percent (default 15.5%, Zimbabwe's 2026 standard rate),
  vat_exempt_education_levels (admin picks which, default none exempt),
  withholding_percent (default 10%, Zimbabwe's common rate for suppliers
  without a ZIMRA tax clearance certificate).
- VAT is computed per order at /api/orders (POST), added as a separate
  tax_cents line on top of the course price (tax-exclusive), shown in the
  checkout summary before payment. It's based on each course's
  education_level against the exemption list, prorated correctly when a
  coupon discount applies. Never touches the instructor/platform split,
  which still runs off the pre-tax price.
- Added per-instructor tax_clearance_number/tax_clearance_expires_at
  (users table), editable from the admin user profile page. Withholding is
  evaluated at payout-approval time using whichever status is current then
  (not whatever it was when each sale happened): a cleared instructor has
  nothing withheld, otherwise withholding_percent is deducted and recorded
  on the payout record (instructor_payouts.gross_cents/withholding_cents,
  amount_cents stays the net amount actually paid). The instructor payouts
  page and the admin payouts list both show this before and after approval.

None of this is legal/tax advice — defaults are deliberately configurable
rather than hardcoded judgment calls, and both admin UI and schema say so.

